A bracketed construct spanning a line boundary

```
See [a
b](/u) here.
.
<p>See <a href="/u">a
b</a> here.</p>
```

```
An [a
b]{.k} span.
.
<p>An <span class="k">a
b</span> span.</p>
```

```
[a
b][r] resolves.

[r]: /u
.
<p><a href="/u">a
b</a> resolves.</p>
```

```
![a
b](/i)
.
<img src="/i" alt="a
b">
```

```
![a
b](/i)
^ A caption.
.
<figure>
  <img src="/i" alt="a
b">
  <figcaption>A caption.</figcaption>
</figure>
```

```
A note ^[a
b] here.
.
<p>A note <a id="fnref1" href="#fn1" role="doc-noteref"><sup>1</sup></a> here.</p>
<section role="doc-endnotes" aria-label="Footnotes">
  <hr>
  <ol>
    <li id="fn1">
      <p>a
b<a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink" aria-label="Back to reference">↩</a></p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>
```

```
:span[a
b] here.
.
<p><span class="ext-span">a
b</span> here.</p>
```

```
An {+a
b+} insertion.
.
<p>An <ins>a
b</ins> insertion.</p>
```

```
A {/a
b/} run.
.
<p>A <em>a
b</em> run.</p>
```
